---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PassportValidityChecker from '../../components/tools/PassportValidityChecker.jsx';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Passport Validity Checker: Is Your Passport Ready for Travel?"
  description="Check if your passport has enough time left for a UK or Schengen trip. Enter your travel and expiry dates, or check another country's official rule."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Passport Validity Checker</h1>
    <p class="mb-8">Will your passport expire too soon for your trip? Choose where you are going and enter your dates to check.</p>
    <PassportValidityChecker client:load />
    <section class="prose max-w-none mt-10">
      <h2>Which travel date should I enter?</h2>
      <p>For the UK or Schengen countries, enter the date you plan to leave that destination. For example, if you visit France and then return to Pakistan, use the date you leave France.</p>
      <p>For a UK visit, your passport must stay valid for the whole stay. For a Schengen visa, it must usually stay valid for at least three months after you leave the Schengen area.</p>
      <h2>Travelling to another country?</h2>
      <p>Check the embassy or official visa website first. Find out how long your passport must stay valid and whether the months are counted from arrival or departure. Choose “Another country” and enter those details. Requirements vary by country, nationality and visa type.</p>
      <h2>What else should I check?</h2>
      <p>Check that you have the right visa, enough spare passport pages and a passport that meets any rules about when it was issued. Also check the rules for countries you pass through. Confirm the full requirements with your embassy and airline.</p>
      <p>The checker counts whole calendar months. If the matching date falls beyond the end of a month, it uses that month's last day.</p>
      <h2>Need to renew your passport?</h2>
      <p>Read our <a href="/guides/pakistan-passport-renewal/">Pakistani passport renewal guide</a> for official fees and how to apply. Allow time for document checks and delivery.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
